==============================================================================
Color rigidity of the ε^abc three-adjoint singlet — exact group theory
==============================================================================

A. The ε contraction is a genuine singlet (total charge annihilates it)
   max |T_total^a |s⟩|  = 0.00e+00   (exact singlet)

B. Pairwise contractions — the only geometry-sensitive color operators
   ⟨s| T_1·T_2 |s⟩ = -1.000000000000  (imag 0.0e+00)
   ⟨s| T_1·T_3 |s⟩ = -1.000000000000  (imag 0.0e+00)
   ⟨s| T_2·T_3 |s⟩ = -1.000000000000  (imag 0.0e+00)
   spread across pairs = 0.00e+00  →  SHAPE-BLIND: every pair
   identical (forced by the permutation antisymmetry of ε — any face
   ordering gives the same state up to sign, so no pairwise operator
   can prefer one geometry over another).

C. Pair channel: which representation each pair sits in
   spectrum of T₁·T₂ on 3⊗3⊗1: [-2. -1.  1.] ...
   3⊗3 = 1 ⊕ 3 ⊕ 5 with T·T = −2, −1, +1. The ε-singlet pair value
   −1 = the ADJOINT channel: each pair binds into an adjoint to meet
   the third face — attractive, but NOT the deepest channel (−2).
   The chain geometry uses the very same contraction: the middle face
   couples the two end strings through the same f^abc = ε^abc vertex.
   Nothing in the algebra forbids it or taxes it.

D. What color CANNOT decide, and what would (class facts, no numbers)
   Adjoint sources in SU(2) are screened by gluons: the adjoint string
   is metastable and breaks at a finite distance set by the gluelump
   mass — a lattice number NOT in the corpus. The recorded spacing is
   d·√σ = c₂ ≈ 1.92. If the SU(2), N_f = 3 breaking distance is below
   that, the string-bound ring of the ADJOINT branch dissolves as a
   long-lived object regardless of geometry — a named exposure for
   that branch (the medium-vortex branch does not carry it).

VERDICT
  1. Candidate (c) FAILS as the ring's stabilizer: the collinear chain
     is color-allowed (same ε vertex), and every pairwise color
     operator is exactly equal across pairs — color is shape-blind at
     two-body order. There is no group-theoretic rigidity to invoke.
  2. Byproduct: the adjoint-branch screening exposure is now named —
     the deciding quantity is the SU(2), N_f = 3 adjoint string-breaking
     distance vs c₂ ≈ 1.92/√σ, one more question for the same lattice
     campaign (with T_c/√σ, F_π/√σ, w·√σ, and the three-source geometry).
  3. Standing after (a), (b), (c): zero-point (b) is the only surviving
     stabilizer, at estimate grade. Ledger rows: (a) and (c).
